    "Notes Updated": "8/16/2025",
    "Scouting Notes": "Starter\n Huge fan of Dorchies\n Think there's a legit 6 pitch mix here with all three FB, two breakers and a splitter\n Big body, probably not a ton of physicality left to be added, but think he can learn to use his body a bit better still and add some velo to a fastball already touching 95 at 18 years old\n Nearly 7 feet of extension helps the velo play up a bit, as does the ride he gets on the fastball from a 3/4 slot\n The four seam is the better fastball at the moment for me, but the sinker could be average or better as well\n The cutter helps keep hitters off of the other fastballs and could be average or better\n I like the slider and how he mixes up shapes and velo on it, I'd personally say it's more like a slider and curve, which is reflected in the tool grades\n The splitter could be a plus pitch\n There's a Kevin Gausman type profile here if he can add some velo\n Long arm action gives some pause in terms of repeatability, but I don't think the walk numbers in Low A are reflective of his command, which I believe will be average or better at his peak",
    "Notes Updated 2": "7/27/2024",
    "Scouting Notes 2": "DRAFT REPORT\nDorchies is being drafted out of Cary Grove HS in Illinois. The UIC commit shows interesting pitch shapes across the board, with a fastball that has some late run to it, a sweeper esque slider, a splitter and a cutter that he showed as a Junior but not much as a senior. My guess is the Brewers will reintroduce the cutter, and potentially even make the fastball into two different pitches (4S and 2S). Velo is in the Upper 80's Low 90's right now, but with his 6'5 frame he seems like a clear candidate for a jump in velo. Interesting arm that likely won't cost them a ton in bonus money given his commitment status to a smaller school.",
